# Bread box 0 (ticket 28.6): the base of the kitchen level, a wooden roll-top bread box 24 x 15.6 x 13.2 m (40 x 26 x 22 cm real, 60 times life size), the same model on both
# sides. Its front (+z) is open towards the middle: the level turns it by yaw 90 (west) and -90 (east); local +z is then world +x and local x is world -z. The origin is the box's
# middle on y = 0, the back wall's outer face at z = -7.8, the front edge at z = 7.8, the side walls' outer faces at x = +-12.
# Inside is one hall 22.8 m wide (x +-11.4) and 12 m high under the roll top, from the back wall's inner face (z = -7.2) to the open front, on a 0.3 m bottom board whose
# front edge is rounded off (a bevel under the bots' 0.4 m step) so the inside joins the worktop. Walls, back and side, are 0.6 m thick. The flag stand goes at (0, 0, -3) (4 m
# in front of the back wall's inner face) and the base health pod at x = +8 (west) or -8 (east), z = -3; half a loaf of bread (kitchen_bread_crust and _bread_crumb, crust wall
# 1.3 m, cover) stands in the back corner at x = -10 and a jam jar at x = +8.8, z = -6 dresses the other. The lid: eighteen slats of the roll top on the deck (y 12 to 12.6, one more at the back) and seven turned
# round the rolled-up top at the back (to 13.2 m, the highest point), with a steel pull at the front; oak caps close the roll's sides. Mesh collider.
# Decision on the slats (28.6): they are split off as the part bread_box_slat (content/parts/kitchen/), 26 uses (18 on the deck, 7 round the roll, 1 behind), as the castle's wall
# bays are (see toy-castle0.sdf): a slat is a plain 23 m bar that would otherwise be meshed 26 times in the body (grooves of 4 cm between them), as a part it is one mesh of 22
# triangles drawn per use through a `draw base` group. The body (walls, board, caps, loaf, jar, pull and straps) is meshed at 256 cells, 3 LODs, about 15k triangles, so the whole box
# is about 16k with every slat, far inside the 80k budget. Only Part uses under translates and turns place the slats.
format 1
collider mesh

